&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking a skilled Network Engineer to join our global team and help&lt;br&gt;design, implement, and maintain our private and public cloud infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;This role involves contributing to the maintenance and operation of network&lt;br&gt;components, with a focus on building smart, scalable, and easy to maintain&lt;br&gt;automated solutions.&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate has experience working in a large-scale enterprise or&lt;br&gt;global cloud service provider network, with strong knowledge of networking&lt;br&gt;principles, and an understanding of networking in AWS, GCP and Azure. They&lt;br&gt;should also be comfortable working in a Linux environment, and proficient at&lt;br&gt;network automation and using configuration management and automation&lt;br&gt;tools such as Git and Ansible. They will possess a good awareness of the&lt;br&gt;network and communications ecosystem and of emerging technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt; Deploy, configure, maintain, troubleshoot and optimize network&lt;br&gt;infrastructure.&lt;br&gt; Collaborate with senior engineers, architecture and engineering teams to&lt;br&gt;implement network requirements and support organisational objectives.&lt;br&gt; Collaborate with external vendors and partners to maintain and continue&lt;br&gt;to improve the network.&lt;br&gt; Contribute to network automation initiatives through the implementation&lt;br&gt;of scalable and intelligent automation solutions.&lt;br&gt; Participate in an on-call rotation to ensure the stability and availability of our&lt;br&gt;critical infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt; 3+ years of experience in a network engineering role, ideally within a large-&lt;br&gt;scale enterprise or cloud service provider network.&lt;br&gt; Strong knowledge of and working experience with network routing,&lt;br&gt;switching, and firewalling.&lt;br&gt; Experience with modern data center network topologies such as spine-and-&lt;br&gt;leaf and overlay networks.&lt;br&gt; Solid understanding of networking principles and concepts, including&lt;br&gt;working knowledge of common protocols such as Ethernet, IP (v4 and v6),&lt;br&gt;TCP, UDP, DNS, IPsec, BGP, VXLAN, EVPN, and HTTPS.&lt;br&gt; Good proficiency in network security, and experience working with NGFW&lt;br&gt;firewalls.&lt;br&gt; Good understanding of public cloud environments (Direct Connect, transit&lt;br&gt;gateway, VPCs, gateway etc.).&lt;br&gt; Strong Grafana proficiency: building and maintaining custom metric&lt;br&gt;exporters and integrating externally provided exporters; designing&lt;br&gt;dashboards; and managing alerting configuration as code, deployed via&lt;br&gt;Terraform.&lt;br&gt; Experience with VPN technologies.&lt;br&gt; Network virtualisation such as VRFs and VXLAN.&lt;br&gt; Ability to perform analysis of network performance and application issues&lt;br&gt;using standard diagnostics tools.&lt;br&gt; Work remotely while collaborating closely with onsite engineers to support&lt;br&gt;network installations, troubleshooting, and maintenance as needed.&lt;br&gt;Desirable Skills (Nice to Have):&lt;br&gt; Experience using and integrating DCIM &amp;amp; IPAM applications, such as&lt;br&gt;Device42, Infoblox etc with automation frameworks.&lt;br&gt; Knowledge of DC networking technologies such as MLAG, Stacking.&lt;br&gt; Experience with cloud providers such as Google Cloud and Azure.&lt;br&gt; CCNA, CCNP, JNCIP-DC, Arista ACE:L3, or similar certification.&lt;br&gt; Proficient working with Linux operating systems.&lt;br&gt; Skilled in scripting (Python or Shell) and familiar with CI/CD practices.&lt;br&gt; Understand concepts of Infrastructure-as-Code/Software.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity, Equity, Inclusion and Belonging (DEIB) &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
